# Allowlist, because the build context is the whole repo and the repo holds
# verbatim guest conversations. `_raw/` carries names, phone numbers and
# arrival dates; `.e2e-vault/` is a full copy of the same after a test run.
# Both are gitignored, which keeps them out of history but not out of a build
# context — every `docker compose build` would otherwise hand the daemon the
# lot, and any later `COPY .` would bake it into a layer.
#
# Deny everything, then name what the Dockerfile copies. A COPY of a path
# missing from this list fails the build, which is the right way round: the
# vault is what must never reach a published image, and it can only get there
# by being named here.
*
!Dockerfile
!docker/cont-init.d/03-link-wiki-skills.sh
!runtime/SOUL.md
!runtime/config.yaml
!runtime/vault-seed
!agent-skills/productivity/property-guest-messaging
!bin
!mcp-seam

# Last match wins, so these come after the allowlist above: a `!bin` that
# re-includes the directory re-includes whatever a local run left in it, and a
# .pyc can carry a value compiled before an edit.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[co]
